# Geodesic thorn testsuite configuration.
#
# Three tests, all integrating the same prograde equatorial circular
# orbit (r = 11.989, M = 2, a = 0.5, Exact = yes, 32 Cactus steps of
# 100 coordinate-time units, one particle):
#
#   circ_orbit           compares the full particle state dump
#                        (t x y z u^t u^x u^y u^z tau) against the
#                        reference data row by row; any change of the
#                        trajectory fails the test.
#
#   circ_orbit_conserved runs the same dump through util/check_conserved,
#                        which prints the Kerr constants of motion
#                        (E, L_z) for every row, and compares those two
#                        columns against the reference; a broken
#                        integrator shows up as a drift of E / L_z.
#
#   circ_orbit_mpi       the same run with 2 MPI ranks.  The
#                        OPTIONS:global integration runs on a single
#                        rank, so the dump must be bit-identical to the
#                        single-rank reference.
#
# The reference files (test/circ_orbit/geodesic_particles.txt,
# test/circ_orbit_conserved/geodesic_particles.txt and
# test/circ_orbit_mpi/geodesic_particles.txt) are the raw dumps of one
# verified run.

EXTENSIONS txt

TEST circ_orbit
{
  RELTOL 1e-12
  NPROCS 1
}

TEST circ_orbit_conserved
{
  POSTPROC check_conserved
  RELTOL 1e-8
  NPROCS 1
}

TEST circ_orbit_mpi
{
  RELTOL 1e-12
  NPROCS 2
}
